"""Approximate an 'os/oz' spelling response, including split word pieces.

Short fragments receive the strongest negative values. Transliteration extends
this rule to other scripts; a final zero can also act like an o. Recent Romance
function words weaken the response, as do familiar whole words. Secondary rules
cover -otic, continuations after os, and paired middle-dot separators.
